+// Turns one Arc profile of an ImportPlan into what the applier writes: rac
+// spaces, pinned lists, favorites, and open tabs, minus what an earlier
+// import already brought. Pure: no profile, no services, no files, so every
+// rule is unit-tested. The applier gathers ArcLiveSidebar, calls
+// MapArcProfile(), and writes the result through SpacesService and
+// SidebarItems.
+//
+// The rules:
+//
+// - Each Arc space becomes its own rac space, keyed by its Arc id. Spaces are
+//   never matched by title, neither with each other nor with a rac space the
+//   user already has.
+// - Pinned lists keep their order. rac's folders are one level deep, so a
+//   folder inside a folder is lifted to the top, right after its parent, and
+//   named by its path, "Parent › Child". A parent left with no tabs of its
+//   own is dropped; an Arc folder that was empty to begin with is kept.
+// - Split views and tab groups are see-through: their tabs take their place
+//   in the list or folder around them.
+// - Open tabs (Today) are flattened to tabs. Only a space this import makes
+//   gets them.
+// - Favorites (Top Apps) are flattened to tabs, and a URL the profile
+//   already has as a favorite isn't added again.
+// - URLs are kept to an allowlist: http, https, file, and about:blank.
+//   Anything else, and anything GURL rejects, is left out and counted.
+// - A rerun skips everything the import record maps, wherever it is now.
+//   New Arc items in a mapped space are appended to it; new tabs in a mapped
+//   folder are appended to that folder. Items whose rac space or folder the
+//   user deleted aren't brought back, and neither are pins or favorites the
+//   user deleted: a rerun adds only what's new in Arc.
+
